Z||000000||sqoach||10-09-2001||05:21 PM||||I just got a 85 GT model kit in the mail that I won on Ebay. It has never been opened (supposedly (said it wasfactory shrink wrap)). I opened it up and found that the trunk lid was missing. I already e-mailed the guy and told him about it just a few minutes ago. This guy has like a ton of positive feedback, and no negative or neutral. I wish it was the indy scoop missing instead. I coulda lived without that.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">            <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||9
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||10-09-2001||05:26 PM||||I would wait and see what he says in the reply e-mail. I would not leave and neg feedback as I am sure he didn't know it was missing<P>Also if you keep it Ray Paulk may have some decklids as he is the toy master contact him at raypaulk@mediaone.net and tell him Josh sent you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||10-09-2001||05:34 PM||||Over the years, every once in a while I've gotten a model kit with a missing part... if you write to the company that made the kit (check the instruction sheet in the kit for a mailing address or phone number), provide them with the kit number, description, and a description and part number of the missing part, they may be able to send you a new part...<P>Yes, it's been a looong time, but you have nothing to lose... I doubt that it's the seller's fault, unless the model kit *wasn't* in fact shrinkwrapped... I mean, what would the guy do with just the decklid piece? <P>Call or write the company - I feel pretty sure they could help you out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
